      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "\"We need food,\" I finally said, the only truce I could muster. I'd go myself. But the pain in my foot was getting worse.",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 128
        }
      ],
      "words": 37
    },
    {
      "block": "原句2",
      "no": 2,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "I hadn't been inside that house, my house, in years, but the staff always kept it stocked. I could bring back food, wine",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 2123
        }
      ],
      "words": 40
    },
    {
      "block": "原句3",
      "no": 3,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "\"It's me. Celia,\" I got out. He breathed in quickly but didn't hang up, which had been my worst fear. \"I think you were ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 9003
        }
      ],
      "words": 36
    },
    {
      "block": "原句4",
      "no": 4,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Still, he was silent. Then a sigh. \"Celia, get your shit together, or don't call.\" And the line went dead",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 9849
        }
      ],
      "words": 20
    },
    {
      "block": "原句5",
      "no": 5,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "He was gone. Mrs. Harper was gone. My parents were gone and you didn't want me",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 9953
        }
      ],
      "words": 16
    },
    {
      "block": "原句6",
      "no": 6,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "He was the problem. I had been—shaken—by the cave, and Harriot's conviction, but I wasn't the catalyst for this tragedy.",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 11208
        }
      ],
      "words": 44
    },
    {
      "block": "原句7",
      "no": 7,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "So Harriot had come after me. She'd crunched through the frozen night, even thrown herself down into that basement after",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 12998
        },
        {
          "text": "and here she was—unmasked, no coat, braving her rabid boar—because she was worried about me. Even after I'd been so awfu",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 13123
        }
      ],
      "words": 45
    },
    {
      "block": "原句8",
      "no": 8,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "I'd been transfixed—briefly—by her gaze as she saw me, and I recognized the look I'd only seen once before, in the cave.",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 20640
        }
      ],
      "words": 40
    }
